From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:11:22 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 04/19] Plutonium: use the Plutonium helper and its agent
 bridge

The thread environment, per-thread X display and pid-to-thread resolver
moved to Plutonium's helper (plutoniumd). The server now asks it for each
thread's setup, and Claude sessions get its MCP server (list, launch,
snapshot, focus, close the thread's windows). The window-threads route is
gone. The web app loads the helper's shell library, and an agent's
focus_window opens the app tab in its thread. ?plutoniumHelper= is read at
boot so the pairing redirect doesn't drop it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
